@segment 20-22 Redridge II & Duskwood I
@start-level 20
# Human Warlock. From the Gnome route's segment 06 (class-neutral Alliance path): same quests, order, binds and
# flights. Changed: all combat hints rewritten for a warlock of level 20-22 (Voidwalker first, DoTs, Fear on
# the second enemy only away from other packs, Drain Life, Health Funnel, Healthstone, Soulstone before the
# hard fights, Sacrifice when it goes wrong; no interrupt, no cure for poison or disease). Segment numbers
# follow this route (the Gnome's segment 7 is segment 08 here, its segment 10 is segment 11). No training stop
# and no warlock class quest in this segment: the level 20 stop and the optional Succubus note are at the end
# of segment 06.
# Carry-in: 119 + 121 (Lakeshire), 455 (Algaz Gauntlet, Menethil in segment 08), 2041 (Shoni in Stormwind),
# 161 (Dun Modr, at 30), 97894 (Auberdine).
# Carry-out: 57, 67, 157, 181, 240, 453 (Duskwood and Westfall, segment 11), 455 (segment 08), 161, 97894.
# Hearth: Thelsamar for the whole segment. It is your way back north at the end, so do not rebind.
# Left out on purpose: 2040 (Deadmines), 126 / 128 / 219 / 180 (level 25-26, segment 11), 19 / 115 / 169 / 248 / 249 (elite),
# 94 (leads to the elite 248), 143-146 and 132 (Westfall bounces).
@carry 119,121,161,455,2041,97894
@done 118,120,125,468

# ---------- Ironforge and Stormwind on the way ----------
FLY Ironforge | Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar
N Look for a Bronze Tube in Ironforge | Viktori in Darkshire needs one Bronze Tube for Look to the Stars. Engineers make it: check the auction house, and ask Gearcutter Cogspinner, the engineering supplier in Tinker Town (67.8, 42.5), on your way to the tram. Not verified: the quest data only lists drops from machines and a vendor in Thousand Needles, so a city supplier stocking one is Classic knowledge. Without a tube you skip the Look to the Stars steps later.
N Take the Deeprun Tram to Stormwind | The tram station is in Tinker Town.
T 2041 | Shoni the Shilent, in the Dwarven District a few steps from the tram exit. Do not take her follow-up (Deadmines). Billibub Cogspinner, the engineering supplier, stands close by (62.4, 29.9): ask him for a Bronze Tube too, and try the Stormwind auction house.
FLY Lakeshire | Dungar Longdrink, the gryphon master in the Trade District

# ---------- Lakeshire ----------
T 119 | Cross the bridge. Verner Osgood, on the town side.
A 122,124 | Verner Osgood
A 98386 | Foreman Oslow at the north end of the bridge: Alther's Mill (new in Forever)
A 20 | Marshal Marris, a few steps east of the bridge
A 98387 @ Redridge Mountains, 28.3, 48.8 | Marshal Marris: Blackrock Blockade (new in Forever)
T 121 | Magistrate Solomon in the town hall
A 91 | Bailiff Conacher, in the town hall too
A 150 | Dockmaster Baren on the dock (needs level 20)
A 34 | Martie Jainrose, the herbalist on the west side of town. Bellygrub is level 24: you kill him last, after the big loop.

# ---------- Loop around Lake Everstill ----------
C 124 @ Redridge Mountains, 24.1, 32.0 | Take the path north out of Lakeshire. Kill 10 Redridge Brutes (17-18, the first camps around 24, 35) and 8 Redridge Mystics (18-19, further up around 24, 29). Send the Voidwalker first. Mystics cast and a warlock has no interrupt: kill them first with Corruption, Curse of Agony, Immolate and Shadow Bolts. Gnolls run at low health: your DoTs finish them. Fear a second gnoll only at the edge of a camp, never inside one. Do not chase Yowler deeper in the hills: that quest is for a later segment.
C 98386 | Go back down and follow the north shore of the lake east to Alther's Mill. Kill 12 Greater Tarantulas (19-20) and destroy 6 Tarantula Eggs around the mill. Send the Voidwalker first and let it take the bites. They poison and a warlock cannot cure it: Drain Life, bandage and eat between fights. Leave Chatter, the rare elite spider that walks here, alone.
C 91 @ Redridge Mountains, 69.0, 50.2 | Keep east into Galardell Valley. Shadowhide gnolls drop the 10 Shadowhide Pendants. Stay at the mouth of the valley, where Rabid Shadowhide Gnolls (21-22) and Shadowhide Gnolls (22-23) stand around 69, 50; the Brutes, Warriors, Slayers and Darkweavers deeper in are 23-26. They are above your level, so some of your spells will be resisted: put a Soulstone on yourself, pull one at a time from far away with the Voidwalker and give it a moment before you start with Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate; then Drain Life. Health Funnel keeps the Voidwalker up. If a second gnoll comes, Fear it only when it would run toward the valley mouth, not deeper in; otherwise back off toward the valley mouth. Eat and drink to full before each pull.
C 20,98387 @ Redridge Mountains, 58.0, 62.0 | From the mouth of the valley go south. Blackrock Grunts (19-20) and Outrunners (20-21) camp on the slopes south-east of the lake, below Stonewatch Keep; Renegades (21-22) are mixed in. They drop the 10 Battleworn Axes. The 8 Stolen Weapons and 10 Blackrock Supplies are in the same camps (new quest: the giver says "south-east below Stonewatch Keep" and the data has no exact spots, so look for things to click in the camps and loot every orc). Stay out of Stonewatch Keep itself: the Scouts, Sentries and Shadowcasters there are elite. Voidwalker first, one orc at a time, all three DoTs, Drain Life when you are hurt. Orcs run for help at low health: your DoTs finish a runner, add a Shadow Bolt. Do not Fear inside a camp.
C 150 @ Redridge Mountains, 47.3, 60.9 | Follow the lake shore back west. Murlocs along the south-east shore (Flesheaters, Tidecallers, Scouts, 18-20) drop the Murloc Fins: you need 8, counting the ones you already carry. As before: single murlocs from the edge of a camp, Voidwalker first, Tidecallers first (they heal and you cannot interrupt), DoTs on every murloc so a runner dies on the way, no Fear on the shore.
C 122 @ Redridge Mountains, 38.6, 67.4 | Black Dragon Whelps (17-18) fly over the hills south of the lake, between the murloc shore and Lakeshire. Kill them until you have 6 Underbelly Whelp Scales. They cast fireballs and you cannot interrupt them: send the Voidwalker so they throw them at it, Health Funnel it, DoT the whelp and wand it down. Drain Soul the last hit when you are short of Soul Shards (keep 3-5), and eat and drink between fights.

# ---------- Lakeshire hand-ins and Bellygrub ----------
T 20 | Back in Lakeshire: Marshal Marris. Do not take the follow-up, Tharil'zun (elite).
T 98387 @ Redridge Mountains, 28.3, 48.8 | Marshal Marris
T 98386 @ Redridge Mountains, 27.1, 48.6 | Foreman Oslow
T 122,124 | Verner Osgood. Do not take Howling in the Hills yet.
T 150 | Dockmaster Baren
T 91 | Bailiff Conacher in the town hall
C 34 | Bellygrub (24), a big boar, roots around in the fields west of Lakeshire, past Martie's garden (10.6, 49.3). He is four levels above you and hits hard: put a Soulstone on yourself, carry a Healthstone and start at full health and mana. Send the Voidwalker and let it hold him for a few seconds, then Corruption, Curse of Agony and Immolate (recast what he resists) and wand or Drain Life; keep Health Funnel on the Voidwalker. If he turns on you, use Sacrifice for the shield and Fear him: the fields around him are empty. If he gets you low, run back toward the town guards.
T 34 | Martie Jainrose

# ---------- Into Duskwood ----------
F Darkshire @ Duskwood, 77.5, 44.3 | Take the road south-west to Three Corners and from there the road south into Duskwood. It leads straight to Darkshire. Stay on the road and keep running: the wolves and spiders beside it are above your level. Felicia Maline, the gryphon master, stands on the east side of town.
A 163,164,165 | Elaine Carevin, at the south end of town
A 56 | Commander Althea Ebonlocke, in front of the town hall
A 96139 @ Duskwood, 72.6, 47.5 | Sirra Von'Indi in the town hall: The Valor Family (new in Forever)
A 101 | Madame Eva, in the house on the north side of the square. You collect her parts over the whole Duskwood trip.
A 174 | Viktori Prism'Antras, in the house at the east end of town. Only with a Bronze Tube in your bags. Without one press Skip here and on every Look to the Stars step that follows in this segment.
T 174 | Viktori Prism'Antras: hand over the Bronze Tube
A 175 | Viktori Prism'Antras
T 175 | Blind Mary lives in the lone house south of Darkshire (82.0, 59.1)
A 177 | Blind Mary. The Insane Ghoul is level 26: you fight him at the end of the segment, when you are back at her house.
C 56 | Tranquil Gardens Cemetery is just south of Mary's house. Kill 8 Skeletal Warriors (21-22) and 6 Skeletal Mages (22-23). Send the Voidwalker first. Mages cast and a warlock has no interrupt: kill them first, all three DoTs and Shadow Bolts; the Voidwalker holds a Warrior meanwhile. Fear a second skeleton only at the edge of the cemetery. Loot everything: they drop Skeleton Fingers for Madame Eva (you need 10). Keep away from the chapel for now, the Insane Ghoul is inside.

# ---------- The south road and Raven Hill ----------
A 245 | Take the road west along the south side of Duskwood. Watcher Dodds stands on it, about halfway (45.1, 67.0). From here on kill the spiders you pass: Pygmy Venom Web Spiders (18-19) count for him, and every spider can drop Vials of Spider Venom for Madame Eva (5) and Gooey Spider Legs. Keep 6 Gooey Spider Legs for a later quest. Let the Voidwalker take the bites: a warlock cannot cure their poison, so Drain Life, bandage and eat. You hand this in when you pass Dodds again.
T 163 | Jitters hides in Raven Hill, the dead village in the west (18.4, 56.4)
A 5 | Jitters
C 96139 @ Duskwood, 18.4, 56.4 | Search Raven Hill for the Raven Hill Tome. New quest: the data has no exact spot, only "search Raven Hill". Look inside the ruined houses and around the village for a book you can click.
T 164 | Sven Yorgen camps on the western edge of Duskwood, north-west of Raven Hill (7.8, 34.1)
A 95 | Sven Yorgen
A 226 | Lars, at the same camp

# ---------- Sven's farm ----------
T 95 | Sven's farm is in the south of the zone, south of Watcher Dodds. Go back along the south road and click the Mound of loose dirt behind the tree stump at the farm (49.9, 77.7). Zzarc'Vul's ogres (around 37, 81, west of the farm) are far above your level: keep away from their mound.
A 230 | From the mound
C 245 | Finish the 15 Pygmy Venom Web Spiders (18-19) in the woods around the farm and along the south road.
T 245 | Watcher Dodds, back on the road north-west of the farm

# ---------- Wolves, the hermit and the cemetery ----------
C 226 @ Duskwood, 30.0, 28.0 | Cut north-west through the woods toward the north side of Raven Hill Cemetery. Kill 12 Starving Dire Wolves (19-20) and 8 Rabid Dire Wolves (20-21): both roam the northern half of western Duskwood.
T 165 | Abercrombie the hermit lives in the shack north of Raven Hill Cemetery (28.1, 31.5)
A 148 | Abercrombie
C 101 @ Duskwood, 23.8, 37.1 | Finish Madame Eva's list. The 10 Ghoul Fangs drop from the ghouls at the east edge of Raven Hill Cemetery, south-west of the shack: Flesh Eaters (24-25) and Rotted Ones (25-26). They are well above you: put a Soulstone on yourself, pull single ghouls out to the edge with the Voidwalker, give it a moment, then DoT (recast what is resisted) and Drain Life; Health Funnel for the Voidwalker. Fight at full health and mana, eat and drink after every pull, and do not go deeper in, where Plague Spreaders and Brain Eaters (27-29) wait. No Fear here: a feared ghoul runs into the cemetery and comes back with more. They spread disease and a warlock cannot cure it: bandage, Drain Life, eat. Skeleton Fingers also drop from Skeletal Horrors (23-24) around Raven Hill, the venom from any spider. If the fangs are too hard at your level, leave the list open: the route is back here in segment 11.
T 230 | Back to Sven Yorgen at his camp
A 262 | Sven Yorgen
T 226 | Lars

